00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:08.320
We're talking about Slalom.

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:13.640
The game was developed by Tim and Chris Stamper, and the music was composed by David Weiss.

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:19.680
Tim and Chris, their brothers, first formed Ultimate Games, which primarily made games

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:23.120
for the ZX Spectrum, which is a British microcomputer.

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:30.200
And Rare came later when they wanted to get into the Japanese video game market.

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:35.320
It was like kind of like... They still had Ultimate, but they figured Rare would be their way of branching off.

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:40.060
Rare is actually the shortened version of Rare Designs of the Future.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:42.500
Wow. That was the full name of the company.

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:44.580
Rare Designs of the Future.

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:46.780
They thought pretty highly of themselves.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.040
They didn't say good designs of the future.

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:50.240
You gotta market yourself. They just said Rare.

00:02:50.380 --> 00:02:57.620
Yeah. And the brothers flew to Kyoto to present software samples to Nintendo executives, like unsolicited.

00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:00.560
Like, they were just like, hey, check out this game.

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:03.640
And Nintendo was like, well, we don't really want to work with you.

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:05.300
And they were like, no, no, no, check out the game.

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:07.760
And then they went to Kyoto and showed it to them.

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:11.180
And Nintendo was like, wow, this is amazing.

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:13.360
Because Slalom is the one there.

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:19.080
They're like seeing like the 3D graphics in the style of like a Mach Rider like thing that only they knew how to do.

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:22.600
So to see someone else pull it off, they said, all right, let's go for it.

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:26.300
And they made, Nintendo kind of made them like their first Western developer.

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:29.820
